title: Field editor
tags: GUI
kind: reference
aliases: field-editor value-widget widget
summary: The input a form shows for a field's value follows the value's type: a number box, a checkbox, a uuid with a pick button, a parent and a name.

The forms that write a value — adding or editing a field in `metarecord-detail`,
the bulk edit of `metarecord-list` — show the same editor: a ''type'' button, and
the input matching the type chosen.

|!Type |!Input |
|`string` |a text field |
|`int` |a number field, whole numbers |
|`float` |a number field |
|`bool` |a checkbox |
|`datetime` |a text field, in ISO-8601 (`2024-03-15T10:30:00Z`) |
|`nothing` |no input: `∅`, the explicit absence |
|`ref` |a uuid, with a 🔍 button opening the [[Value picker]] |
|`tree_ref` |a parent uuid (empty for a root) with its 🔍 button, then the name |
|`refbase` |a uuid, with a 🔍 button |
|`externalref` |a repository uuid and a metarecord uuid |

The type button offers the first eight. `refbase` and `externalref` are not offered
for a new value; they are edited where a value of that type already exists.

For a field name that already has a type in the repository, the button offers that
type and `nothing` only: a value can always be replaced by an explicit absence. A new
name is offered every type.

The button opens a menu of the GUI rather than the system's drop-down: the forms sit
at the bottom of a panel, where the system's list opens downwards, off the window.

!! In the command input

The `metarecord:field` and `metarecord:bulk` commands take a value on one line
instead:

|!Type |!Written |
|`string` |as is |
|`int`, `float` |the number |
|`bool` |`true` or `false` (completed) |
|`datetime` |the ISO-8601 text |
|`ref` |a uuid — or a candidate of the completion, which names the target and stands for its uuid ([[Completion views]]) |
|`tree_ref` |a path in the field's tree, `music/jazz`: the last piece is the name, what precedes names the parent |

The editor is `panel-shim/value-widget.js`, served as `/__value-widget.js`
(`createTypePicker`, `widgetFor`, `parseRawValue`).
